{"seconds": 145.3, "exit": 0, "final": "**Best move:** Nf7\n\n**Main line:** Nf7 Ng3+ Qxg3 Kxf7 Qxg5\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nYour knight on e5 delivers a fork, attacking both the bishop on g5 and the rook on f8 simultaneously. Black's only try to create counterplay is Ng3+, forcing your queen to capture: after Qxg3, Black's king must take on f7 (Kxf7), but then the bishop falls undefended to Qxg5. You win a full bishop\u2014a decisive material advantage. The key lesson: when you have a forcing sequence (a check or capture), calculate it completely before moving. A knight fork that draws the defender into a worse position is often the most elegant way to win material.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf7\", \"line\": [\"Nf7\", \"Ng3+\", \"Qxg3\", \"Kxf7\", \"Qxg5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Ng6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p3N1p/p1p1p3/2Pn1pb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K b - - 1 24", "move": "Nxf2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Nd7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5